s://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99002","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99002","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99002.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99002.patch","merged_at":"2024-11-12T18:19:41Z"},"body":"Continuation of #95774\r\nSee also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89036\r\n\r\nThis PR addressed yet another huge chunk of class reference oddities I remembered to note down for later while localizing the class reference. Some of these are clear typos, some are inconsistencies, some are just awkward.\r\n\r\nI decided to separate this from the original because these may be more prickly.\r\n\r\nOf particular note:\r\n- Fix some things that were fixed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89036 but came back in full force because I cannot be behind every contributor's back.\r\n- **PROPERTY_USAGE_CLASS_IS_ENUM** called the property an \"enum\", whereas it's probably closer to an [enum type variable](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-language/c-enumeration-declarations?view=msvc-170), which is less ambiguous.\r\n- Replace the few uses of \"_acquire_\", \"_interrogate_\", and \"_augment_\" with more common verbs.\r\n- Replace leftover references to \"spatial node\" from 3.x.\r\n- **NEVER** write \"_The node (and any relevant children) should be [member CanvasItem.visible]_\" ever again. I'm going to cry.\r\n\r\nFor the descriptions affected, not many tweaks have been made this time. Who knows when this will be merged anyway.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/